wifi: iwlwifi: mld: let a large reorder buffer come from vmalloc

iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start() allocates the session data and a reorder
buffer per RX queue in one kzalloc(). With many RX queues and a large
block-ack window that reaches an order-5 allocation, which a machine
whose memory has been up a while often can't find contiguous. The
allocation then fails with a page allocation failure warning, the
ADDBA request is refused, and the link runs that TID without
aggregation.

The XPS 14 DA14260 (BE211) logged four such failures at order 5 in one
day on 7.3.4, from cfg80211_wiphy_work through
ieee80211_process_addba_request, one a second after a roam. Each time
the Normal zone held free pages, but no free block of 128 kB or larger.

The buffers are only read and written by the CPU, never by the device,
so they needn't be physically contiguous. Allocate them with
kvzalloc(), which tries kmalloc first and falls back to vmalloc, and
free them with kvfree() and kvfree_rcu().

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/agg.c b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/agg.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/agg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/agg.c
@@ -551,11 +551,17 @@ int iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start(struct iwl_mld *mld, struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 	reorder_buf_size = ALIGN(reorder_buf_size, SMP_CACHE_BYTES);
 
 	/* Allocate here so if allocation fails we can bail out early
-	 * before starting the BA session in the firmware
+	 * before starting the BA session in the firmware.
+	 *
+	 * The reorder buffers are only ever read by the CPU, and with many
+	 * RX queues and a large window they reach an order-5 allocation,
+	 * which a fragmented machine often can't find contiguous: the
+	 * session is then refused and the link runs without aggregation.
+	 * kvzalloc() falls back to vmalloc for those.
 	 */
-	baid_data = kzalloc(sizeof(*baid_data) +
-			    mld->trans->info.num_rxqs * reorder_buf_size,
-			    GFP_KERNEL);
+	baid_data = kvzalloc(sizeof(*baid_data) +
+			     mld->trans->info.num_rxqs * reorder_buf_size,
+			     GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!baid_data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
@@ -605,7 +611,7 @@ int iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start(struct iwl_mld *mld, struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 	return 0;
 
 out_free:
-	kfree(baid_data);
+	kvfree(baid_data);
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -642,7 +648,7 @@ int iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_stop(struct iwl_mld *mld, struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 	iwl_mld_free_reorder_buffer(mld, baid_data);
 
 	RCU_INIT_POINTER(mld->fw_id_to_ba[baid], NULL);
-	kfree_rcu(baid_data, rcu_head);
+	kvfree_rcu(baid_data, rcu_head);
 
 	IWL_DEBUG_HT(mld, "BAID %d is free\n", baid);
 
